[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Keyboard shortcuts (/guides/keyboard-shortcuts)\n\nThese are the current defaults. On Mac, open **Settings → Shortcuts** to search the whole catalog, record a new shortcut, clear an assignment, inspect conflicts, or restore the default. Commands marked **Unassigned** remain available from the menu and command palette.\n\n## Windows and navigation [#windows-and-navigation]\n\n| Action | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| New Window | Command-N |\n| New Blank Window (Mac) | Option-Command-N |\n| New Tab | Command-T |\n| New Quick Window (Mac) | Option-Shift-Command-N |\n| New Private Window | Shift-Command-N |\n| Close Current Tab or Window | Command-W |\n| Close Window | Shift-Command-W |\n| Open Location / command palette | Command-L |\n| Back | Command-[ |\n| Forward | Command-] |\n| Reload Page | Command-R |\n| Stop Loading | Command-. |\n| Reload from Origin | Shift-Command-R |\n\nOn Mac, **Command-L** opens the address editor while keeping a collapsed sidebar collapsed.\n\n## Tabs and Spaces [#tabs-and-spaces]\n\n| Action | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| Pin or Unpin Current Tab | Command-D |\n| Duplicate Tab | Unassigned |\n| Reopen Last Closed Tab | Shift-Command-T |\n| Clear Unpinned Tabs | Shift-Command-K |\n| Archive Tab | Command-E |\n| Previous Tab | Option-Command-Up Arrow |\n| Next Tab | Option-Command-Down Arrow |\n| Most Recent Tab | Control-Tab |\n| Most Recent Tab Backward | Control-Shift-Tab |\n| Select Tab 1–9 | Command-1 through Command-9 |\n| Previous Space | Option-Command-Left Arrow |\n| Next Space | Option-Command-Right Arrow |\n| Select Space 1–9 | Control-1 through Control-9 |\n\nTap **Control-Tab** to jump to the tab you used last. On a Mac, hold it to see your recent tabs: press **Tab** or the arrow keys to move through them and let go of **Control** to switch. **Control-Shift-Tab** goes to the tab you used longest ago. A split appears as one card. To skip the previews, turn off **Show recent tabs while switching** in Settings > Tabs.\n\n## Split View [#split-view]\n\n| Action | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| Split With Next Tab | Unassigned |\n| Focus Previous Split Card | Control-Command-Left Arrow |\n| Focus Next Split Card | Control-Command-Right Arrow |\n| Remove Tab From Split | Unassigned |\n| Separate All Tabs | Option-Command-U |\n| Move Split Card Left | Shift-Command-Left Arrow |\n| Move Split Card Right | Shift-Command-Right Arrow |\n\n## Page tools [#page-tools]\n\n| Action | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| Show or Hide Reader | Unassigned |\n| Show or Hide Translation Toolbar | Shift-Command-L |\n| Toggle Content Blocking | Unassigned |\n| Find in Page | Command-F |\n| Zoom In | Command-+ |\n| Zoom Out | Command-- |\n| Actual Size | Command-0 |\n| Copy Page Link | Shift-Command-C |\n| Copy Page Link as Markdown | Option-Shift-Command-C |\n| Share Page | Unassigned |\n| Export as PDF | Unassigned |\n| Save Web Archive | Unassigned |\n| Print Page | Command-P |\n\n## Browser surfaces and developer tools [#browser-surfaces-and-developer-tools]\n\n| Action | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| Show or Hide Sidebar | Command-S |\n| Show History | Command-Y |\n| Show Archive | Unassigned |\n| Show Downloads | Shift-Command-J |\n| Show Web Inspector | Option-Command-I |\n| Show or Hide Developer Toolbar (Mac) | Shift-Command-I |\n\n## iPad hardware keyboards [#ipad-hardware-keyboards]\n\niPad uses Crest’s shipped defaults for the commands available on that platform. Hold the Command key to inspect commands exposed by the current menu context. Full shortcut rebinding is a Mac feature.\n\nOn iPad, **Option-Command-N** remains New Quick Window. New Blank Window is a Mac command.\n\n## Context-only keys [#context-only-keys]\n\nSome temporary interfaces have their own local actions. In Peek, **Command-W** closes the preview and **Command-O** promotes it to a full tab. **Escape** dismisses transient panels such as the command palette or Quick Window flow when dismissal is available.\n\n## Resolve a conflict on Mac [#resolve-a-conflict-on-mac]\n\nSearch for either command in **Settings → Shortcuts**, select the row, and record a different key combination. Crest shows collisions before the replacement becomes part of your command map. Clearing a shortcut makes the action unassigned; resetting restores the shipped default.\n"]
